      },
      {
        "heading_raw": "Benefit",
        "body_raw": "When wielding a rapier one-handed, you can add your Dexterity modifier instead of your Strength modifier to that weapon’s damage. The rapier must be one appropriate for your size. You do not gain this benefit while fighting with two weapons or using flurry of blows, or anytime another hand is otherwise occupied. In addition, if you have the panacheACG class feature, you gain a +2 bonus to your CMD against attempts to disarm you of your rapier while you have at least 1 panache point."
      }
